"EEG driven seizure classification framework leveraging variational mode decomposition technique and entropy features based Bayesian optimized SVM - ScienceDirect (https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0960077925007921)\nciteturn20search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.1 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; Volume 199, Part 3, October 2025, 116779 ... Another under-explored research domain in the ML based seizure diagnosis is the potential of entropy features.\n\n## Chaos, Solitons & Fractals\n\nVolume 199, Part 3, October 2025, 116779\n\n# EEG driven seizure classification framework leveraging variational mode decomposition technique and entropy features based Bayesian optimized SVM\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1016/j.chaos.2025.116779Get rights and content\n\n## Highlights\n\n  * •\n\nA novel EEG driven BOSVM classifier framework for seizure classification is presented.\n\n  * •\n\nThe subtle variations in EEG signals are extracted using VMD technique and entropy features.\n\n  * •\n\nOptimal entropy features are chosen based on NCA and ReliefF algorithms.\n\n  * •\n\nThe class imbalance problem is addressed using ADASYN technique.\n\n## Abstract\n\nEEG signal can capture spatial and temporal shifts in electrical activity of the brain, thereby acting as a prominent biomarker to diagnose seizure. Nevertheless, as EEG recordings are generally high-dimensional and noisy, manual examination of any such abnormalities in EEG patterns to diagnose seizure is a time consuming and tedious task for a neurologist. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHolt–Winters smoothing enhanced by fruit fly optimization algorithm to forecast monthly electricity consumption - ScienceDirect (https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0360544219324740)\nciteturn20search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6.7 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; Volume 193, 15 February 2020, 116779 ... 2020, Entropy\n\nVolume 193, 15 February 2020, 116779\n\n# Holt–Winters smoothing enhanced by fruit fly optimization algorithm to forecast monthly electricity consumption\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1016/j.energy.2019.116779Get rights and content\n\n## Highlights\n\n  * •\n\nIt is the first attempt to enhance the Holt–Winters exponential smoothing method.\n\n  * •\n\nA high forecasting accuracy can be obtained by FOA-MHW method for the monthly electricity consumption.\n\n  * •\n\nThe proposed FOA-MHW method can obtain incredible performance even in the situation of insufficient training data.\n\n  * •\n\nThe proposed FOA-MHW model has the shortest execution time among with all the other hybrid models.\n\n## Abstract\n\nElectricity consumption forecasting is essential for intelligent power systems. In fact, accurate forecasting of monthly consumption to predict medium- and long-term demand substantially contributes to the appropriate dispatch and management of electric power systems. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n18H05450 研究成果報告書 (https://kaken.nii.ac.jp/ja/file/KAKENHI-ORGANIZER-18H05450/18H05450seika.pdf)\nciteturn20search12 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 11 months ago; <tr><td>Tensile and compressive plastic deformation behavior of medium entropy Cr-Co-Ni single crystals from cryogenic to elevated temperatures</td><td>2022</td></tr> ... <tr><td>Acta Materialia</td><td>116779 116779</td></tr>\n<table id=\"e1\">\n<tr><td>Li Le Chen Zhenghao Kuroiwa Shogo Ito Mitsuhiro Kishida Kyosuke Inui Haruyuki George Faso P.</td><td>148</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Tensile and compressive plastic deformation behavior of medium entropy Cr-Co-Ni single crystals from cryogenic to elevated temperatures</td><td>2022</td></tr>\n<tr><td>International Journal of Plasticity</td><td>103144 103144</td></tr>\n<tr><td>DOI<br>10.1016/j.ijplas.2021.103144</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<table id=\"e2\">\n<tr><td>Kishida Kyosuke Nakatsuka Satoshi Nose Hiroaki Inui Haruyuki</td><td>223